<title>UK: BT, MCI deal will not harm UK competition--govt.</title>
<headline>BT, MCI deal will not harm UK competition--govt.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The proposed merger between British Telecommunications Plc and MCI Communications Corp should not harm development of competition in the UK telecommunications industry, the government said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The Government...considers in particular that the merged company should not pose a threat to the future development of competition in the UK,&quot; it wrote in its response to a report on the industry by parliament's Trade and Industry Committee.</p>
</text>
